  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is individuals who engage with social media platforms and are familiar with the interface and language of online content interaction, particularly those who may be prone to expressing strong, impulsive, or aggressive reactions to online content. The meme is designed to appeal to users who might be seeking to vent frustration or express disapproval in an exaggerated, violent manner, by invoking the ultimate symbol of historical evil (Adolf Hitler) to justify their reaction. The meme's effectiveness relies on the audience's recognition of the social media phrase 'I don't like this post' and their ability to interpret the visual-textual juxtaposition as a darkly humorous or provocative statement, thereby normalizing the idea that extreme violence is an appropriate response to online content. The target community is not defined by specific demographics but by their engagement with digital discourse and their susceptibility to the meme's hateful, dehumanizing message.",
